# because a budget nobody tightens decays into a rubber stamp.
#
# ── T-181.13.1 (2026-07-25): the debt these numbers marked is PAID ─────────────────────────────
# The wave-5 adversarial verifier proved 27 warnings across the four goldens, of which 2 were
# correct. Cause: the JsonLoadContext landmine in TBD_MissionValidator.CheckSlotLoadout —
# `slot.loadout` and `loadout.gear` are `ref <class>` fields that JsonLoadContext allocates even
# when the JSON key is ABSENT, so every loadout-less slot was reported as "loadout.gear is present
# but every gear ref is empty", and the "neither gear nor cargo" branch was unreachable dead code.
#
# CheckSlotLoadout now tests CONTENT (gear ref count, cargo row count) — the same content test
# T-181.32 settled on for TBD_SpawnManager.HasAuthoredLoadout — and only claims a loadout is
# "present" where that is provable. Measured on the same live boots, and NEW: a `ref array<>` field,
# UNLIKE a `ref <class>` one, comes back NULL when its key was absent. So `loadout.cargo != null` is
# a real presence test, and it is the one thing that can tell an authored-but-empty loadout from no
# loadout at all.
#
#   msn_8f3a2c  18 -> 0   every one was spurious; no slot in that mission authors a `loadout` key
#   msn_0e77ab   7 -> 2   the two slots authoring `"cargo": []`, i.e. an empty loadout block —
#                         exactly what the dead branch was written to report. The website compiler
#                         cannot emit that shape (crates/map-engine-core/src/mission/flatten.rs
#                         skips empty gear and empty cargo and drops an all-empty loadout), so on a
#                         real mission it means the JSON was hand-edited.
#   msn_5c1de7   2 -> 0   one spurious, one legal cargo-only loadout misdiagnosed as empty gear
#   msn_2d91be   1 -> 1   unrelated to loadouts: that fixture has no slots[] at all
#
# These are no longer a debt marker — they are the floor. Every remaining warning is one somebody
# should act on. Tighten again on any further fall.
#
